name issue_62_audio_only_probing
describe Audio-only call on a clean 1 Mbps link: the initial probes are not capped by the audio allocation, and the audio stream asks for ALR probes (issue #62)
# On the base commit the session told GoogCC the audio allocation (about 52 kbps on the wire)
# before it started, so the initial probes were capped at twice that (104 kbps) and the
# estimate fell to the probe result and the acknowledged audio rate. libwebrtc's GoogCC is
# created when the network comes up, before AudioSendStream::Start registers its bitrate, so
# its 900 kbps and 1.8 Mbps probes go out once an audio packet of 200 bytes is queued
# (BitrateProber), and AudioSendStream with transport-cc asks for ALR probes every 5 s.
duration 30s
video off
at 0s capacity=1000kbps delay=40ms
# Base commit: 135-144 kbps on seeds 1-5; this change: 189-265 (libwebrtc: see the PR's compare-webrtc job).
expect cc.target_avg_kbps > 170
expect audio.concealed_pct < 1
expect audio.interruptions == 0
